{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said further to Moses: Thus shall you say to the children of Israel.</b> It is not fitting that they call Me by My special name for all their needs and affairs — all the more so than a man of flesh and blood, who is not called by his name, but rather thus they shall call Me by the name HaShem, the Elohim of your fathers, which is an expression of lordship and sovereignty, just as one says, 'Long live the king.'" "<b>HaShem, the Elohim of your fathers, the Elohim of Abraham.</b> From here [we learn] that we say in the Amida: 'Our Elohim and the Elohim of our fathers, the Elohim of Abraham, the Elohim of Isaac, and the Eloheim of Jacob.' (Mekhilta.)" "<b>This is My name.</b> The 'אהיה' stated in the first verse is <b>My name forever</b>, for thus we write the special name with the letters mem-tzadi-peh-tzadi, for the Holy One, blessed be He, calls Himself tzadi-mem-peh-tzadi, and we call Him mem-tzadi-peh-tzadi. That is: He is now and afterward without end. And the vav of mem-tzadi-peh-tzadi stands in place of yod, like the vav of 'הוה גביר,' which stands in place of yod, and it is like 'היה.' And because it is not proper that this word of sacred existence be like the rest of the words of profane existence, it is distinguished from the rest of the words of profane existence." "<b>And this is My memorial for all generations.</b> That which is stated in the second verse — 'the Elohim of your fathers' — in the manner that one mentions kings, and not by their special name."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "Comment 1 cites Mekhilta; per voice rules (compiler gathers without naming sources), but the parenthetical '(מכילתא)' appears in the source text itself, so it is rendered as found. Comment 2: Chizkuni uses a cipher of the divine-name letters; the cipher and its explanation are rendered literally as they stand, preserving his letter-name terminology."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:06.020581457Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}